stateDiagram-v2
  %% Today's code (the "current" design of AcpSessionStaysOpen.tla), as the person sees a session.
  %% Drawn from TLC's shortest counterexamples for the three rules it breaks, and from the model's actions.
  [*] --> OpenAlone
  state "Open, only the opener" as OpenAlone
  state "Open, the opener and followers" as OpenWithFollowers
  state "Turn running" as Running
  state "Turn asks the opener for permission" as Asking
  state "Closed, followers still listed" as ClosedListed
  state "Closed, nobody listed" as ClosedEmpty

  OpenAlone --> OpenWithFollowers : a follower joins
  OpenAlone --> Running : the opener sends a prompt
  OpenWithFollowers --> Running : a client sends a prompt
  Running --> OpenWithFollowers : the turn ends with followers
  Running --> OpenAlone : the turn ends alone
  Running --> Asking : the turn asks for permission
  Asking --> Running : the opener answers
  OpenWithFollowers --> OpenWithFollowers : a follower leaves and another stays
  OpenWithFollowers --> ClosedListed : the opener sends session/close or its input ends
  Running --> ClosedListed : the opener leaves during the turn
  Asking --> ClosedListed : the opener leaves while the question waits
  ClosedListed --> ClosedListed : a follower leaves and another stays
  ClosedListed --> ClosedEmpty : the last follower leaves
  OpenAlone --> ClosedEmpty : the opener sends session/close

  note right of ClosedListed
    BROKEN: StaysOpenWhileMember and OneMainInJoinOrder (the closing and successor rules of Following a session)
    BROKEN: DeniedOnlyWhenNoMember, when the question was open (a question is denied only when no member remains)
    Shortest path to StaysOpen and OneMain: start, a follower joins, the opener sends session/close (3 steps)
    Shortest path to DeniedOnly: start, a follower joins, the opener sends a prompt, the turn asks, the opener leaves (5 steps)
  end note
  note right of ClosedEmpty
    Nothing is broken here: no member and no session, so the session is closed as the closing rule of Following a session says
  end note
